# Public, browser-safe values only.
# Anything VITE_-prefixed is compiled into the browser bundle, so it is
# readable by anyone who loads the site. The publishable key belongs here.
#
# Secrets never go in this file -- it is tracked in git. The service_role
# key and any Supabase personal access token go in .env.local, which
# .gitignore excludes via *.local, and in the Vercel dashboard.

# Public by design, and committed on purpose.
#
# Vite compiles VITE_* variables into the browser bundle, so neither of these
# can be secret: anyone can read them out of the deployed JavaScript. Row Level
# Security is what separates one person's training history from another's, not
# the obscurity of this key. See the Backend rules in CLAUDE.md.
#
# Keeping them here rather than in the Vercel dashboard means Preview and
# Production cannot drift apart, and a fresh clone builds a working app.
# .env.local still overrides this file locally and stays gitignored, which is
# where anything genuinely secret would go.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://qnnqnyptmhznlfiszvtn.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_kwIAMCVfP_IwLs_TWr4PdA_73bRpsma
